</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Chronic hepatitis D: a vanishing disease? An italian multicenter study.</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><volume>32</volume><fpage>824</fpage><lpage>827</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11003629</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005247-Martcheva1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martcheva</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pilyugin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Holt</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Subthreshold and superthreshold coexistence of pathogen variants: the impact of host age-structure.</article-title><source>Math Biosci</source><volume>207</volume><fpage>58</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17087980</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005247-Niro1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Niro</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosina</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rizzeto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Treatment of hepatitis D.</article-title><source>J Viral Hepat</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>2</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15655042</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005247-May1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nowak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Superinfection, metapopulation dynamics, and the evolution of diversity.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>170</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid"